WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:03.959
You've all finished the game at this point. Right? Right?

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:12.210
So I've decided to compile my last 50 secrets for Sekiro into one video instead of three because

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:14.819
after this, it might be time to move on

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:17.400
Let's begin with what might be the best

00:00:17.529 --> 00:00:18.910
secret on this list

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:26.820
In the Shura ending, Owl orders wolf to forsake his master with the intent to take Kuro away from the lands of the Ashina.

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:33.149
What ensues is a conflict between Wolf, Emma and then Isshin. And it's a conflict that Owl

00:00:33.579 --> 00:00:36.089
excuses himself from just before the battle.

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:43.110
But did you ever wonder why Owl left here and what he might be doing as you cut down isshin and Emma?

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:49.799
The answer is incredibly subtle, but it's hidden within this scene. See if you can hear it.

00:00:52.239 --> 00:00:54.070
That soft

00:00:54.070 --> 00:01:01.289
Squelching thud is very suspect. It seems like owl is putting something down right beside Isshin's corpse.

00:01:01.289 --> 00:01:06.569
Right? This led me to ask Lance McDonald, prominent Souls born data digger

00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:12.180
to disconnect the camera in this cutscene and see if there was anything to find and sure enough

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:19.589
The thing that Owl puts down beside Isshin is the severed head of Isshin's grandson, Genichiro

00:01:19.689 --> 00:01:26.999
so while you were dealing with Emma and Isshin. Owl stepped away and assassinated Genichiro. Why? Well

00:01:27.159 --> 00:01:33.449
Genichiro is also competing for Kuro's blood, plus Owl also returns with the black mortal blade

00:01:33.759 --> 00:01:39.419
Meaning that Genichiromust have located it at this point in the game. Black mortal blade in hand

00:01:39.670 --> 00:01:41.670
Very little should stand in Owl's way

00:01:42.369 --> 00:01:45.269
except Shura, of course who ironically

00:01:45.909 --> 00:01:49.949
might have been awakened by the carnage that Owl initiated.

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:56.640
As that dialogue reveals, Owl's real name is Usui, which links him to a place called

00:01:56.640 --> 00:02:01.700
Usui's forest, a mystical place mentioned in two item descriptions.

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:07.120
First it's mentioned in the mist Raven feathers, belonging to one of the many mystical birds that reside within

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:11.190
Usui's forest and second in the phantom kunai item, which

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:17.100
reveals that Lady Butterfly trained in Owl's forest since childhood. A place filled with mist and

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:21.780
mystifications which somewhat explains the shinobi that Owl became,

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:27.629
In our first fight with Owl he'll recite different parts of the shinobi code after each death

00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:32.010
we experienced at his hand. First: that the parent is absolute and

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:38.790
If you unlocked a second resurrection during the fight by performing a death blow then you hear that

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:46.100
Second: the master is absolute. But what very few people know is that there's a third rule, one

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:53.360
That's never mentioned unless you unlock a third resurrection by consuming a Jizo statue during the fight.

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:55.820
Three: Fear is absolute

00:02:55.820 --> 00:03:01.880
There is no shame in losing one battle, but you must take revenge by any means necessary,

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:07.409
No wonder if you've got it in you to bring me down

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:13.280
It's no surprise that Owl is one of Miyazaki's favorite bosses in Sekiro

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:20.100
Before launch he gave this interview where he stated that his favorite boss uses really dirty underhanded

00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:24.989
Tricks and that they're devious and that he hopes that we'll know it when we see it

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:29.880
It has to be Owl right for this fight has this fantastic flavor to it

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:35.249
it's a boss that knows how to disable our heal, one that can use Mikiri and

00:03:35.890 --> 00:03:41.520
Most impressive to me. He's the first boss that actually has trickery just built into his animations

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:43.470
He starts feigning attacks

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:48.990
Just as soon as you get used to countering them. His gameplay mechanics reflect his character design

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:53.340
Which I think is a really worthwhile design goal for any developer.

00:03:54.060 --> 00:04:00.580
Up here, as Ashina castle is being besieged by the interior ministry the soundtrack takes a bit of a turn

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:04.020
Listen to this part and tell me if anything sounds familiar

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:15.939
You guessed it. That strained sound is the same one that we heard back in the 10-second shadows die twice teaser.

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:23.649
In this same area earlier in the game. We fight Genichiro and we see his second phase here, the way of Tomoe.

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:26.860
But did you ever wonder why he strips his metal arm off here

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:33.159
It could be because his flesh is astoundingly resilient. Anyway, thanks to the rejuvenating settlement

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:39.459
It could be that the way of Tomoe favors flowing unhindered movement. Well my favorite idea

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:43.060
is that his metal armor might conduct electricity and

00:04:43.730 --> 00:04:46.420
Things are about to get heretical up in here

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:48.650
To prepare for the invasion

00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:54.910
Warriors of the Ashina pour over a map within the Ashina dojo. The map depicts the area that you're in right now

00:04:55.400 --> 00:05:02.560
Here's the main castle, the lake, the path to the Sunken Valley, to the outskirts and back down the main road.

00:05:02.810 --> 00:05:10.179
Just around the corner from this map is a tiny little shrine on the wall, one that's dedicated to what can only be the Divine

00:05:10.190 --> 00:05:16.660
Dragon. Its distinctive face is recognizable as is the body twisted around the stump of the sakura tree

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:19.900
Attached we see what looked like omikuji

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:25.450
Little requests for blessings that are written on paper by the occupants of the castle

00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:29.439
And did you ever wonder how certain shinobi doors work most of them make sense?

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:37.390
Simply taking you from one room to the next but some of them make as much sense as traveling in Dark Souls 2

00:05:37.910 --> 00:05:40.689
from the earthen peak to the iron keep

00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:44.770
After taking an elevator that is to say it makes no sense

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:48.520
To flip a door in Ashina castle and end up in the dilapidated

00:05:48.770 --> 00:05:55.689
Temple. Nor to flip the door in headless' cave and end up deep within the mountains of Senpou Temple

00:05:56.120 --> 00:06:02.049
However From has put one tiny little detail here to deter any naysayers. There are nine

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:06.520
Unintelligible ancient Japanese symbols on the ground in both of these places

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:10.299
Which we can only surmise to be magic markings

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:17.819
Controlling these shinobi doors, allowing us to teleport from one place to another and as you all know if it's magic

00:06:18.099 --> 00:06:20.099
It ain't gotta explain shit

00:06:20.919 --> 00:06:26.249
Right besides some of the smallest most impressive details often lie

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:30.750
The most egregious mistakes that no lore master wants to bother trying to explain.

00:06:31.389 --> 00:06:36.059
For example, the so-called secret path out of Ashina doesn't really deliver

00:06:36.610 --> 00:06:39.810
Considering it's just an open field with a broken bridge

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:45.509
Going nowhere. I'm not exactly sure why Sekiro and Kuro keep coming back here.

00:06:45.699 --> 00:06:48.119
However in this very same area

00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:52.109
We also see some of the best hidden details that this game

00:06:52.210 --> 00:06:57.120
has to offer. In our first fight with Genichiro, Wolf is fighting after having

00:06:57.340 --> 00:07:02.969
experienced a complete defeat having only recently lost his will to live, thus he's

00:07:03.099 --> 00:07:10.019
completely out of practice and his skills here are really rusty and it's shown visually in this cutscene actually.

00:07:10.020 --> 00:07:13.049
Look at how Sekiro actually fumbles for his sword

00:07:13.360 --> 00:07:17.939
Before he pulls it out, compare this to the Sekiro who fights at the end of the game

00:07:18.009 --> 00:07:21.689
Look how smoothly he pulls out his sword and prepares for combat

00:07:22.180 --> 00:07:29.400
Not only that, but this wisp of grass here actually represents Kuro who has just fallen to the ground behind him

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:32.459
It's something that Sekiro doesn't even notice

00:07:32.669 --> 00:07:38.908
That's how focused he is on the looming fight with Genichiro. Moving from Ashina into the depths

00:07:39.069 --> 00:07:41.759
We encounter our first Shichimen Warrior

00:07:41.889 --> 00:07:43.750
Which in Japanese means?

00:07:43.750 --> 00:07:49.889
The warrior with seven faces. His design lives up to that, as he has a ton of faces all over his armor and

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:55.529
Attacks with spirit heads that inflicts terror. This warrior in particular drops the Ceremonial Tanto,

00:07:55.529 --> 00:07:59.039
Which is a dagger that was used in ritual offerings to the Divine Dragon.

00:07:59.169 --> 00:08:06.179
They would cut spirit emblems from their own flesh. And as we know spirit emblems harbor the souls of the dead

00:08:06.819 --> 00:08:14.309
Considering this warrior harbors many lost souls himself. It's an item and a task that really suits this warrior

00:08:14.919 --> 00:08:19.318
Curiously, their armor also features reared up centipedes on the shoulder guards

00:08:19.629 --> 00:08:24.778
The centipedes are representative of the depraved immortality of the Fountainhead waters

00:08:24.849 --> 00:08:30.909
So it does make some sense that these warriors who once made blood offerings to those waters

00:08:31.100 --> 00:08:34.840
Would seek to adorn their armor with their likeness

00:08:35.050 --> 00:08:38.950
In fact most characters with centipedes can trace their immortality

00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:46.629
to the fountain headwaters. Take the Guardian Ape for example who in addition to lurking in a location where the fountain

00:08:46.820 --> 00:08:53.530
Headwaters pull deeply also soothes its severed head wound in a small waterfall of flowing with these same

00:08:53.720 --> 00:09:00.850
Fountainhead waters and as the centipede erupts from the Apes body take special note of the way that the Apes movement changes

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:04.749
Originally it fights like a beast as its original self

00:09:04.760 --> 00:09:12.189
But in the second phase the centipede actually takes control and now it fights with writhing centipede-like winding attacks

00:09:12.680 --> 00:09:15.609
furthermore it learns how to use a weapon which

00:09:16.070 --> 00:09:20.739
Raises even more questions about the centipedes and just how intelligent they really are

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:23.739
The Apes waters are Fountainhead waters

00:09:23.740 --> 00:09:25.600
Which is a fact that's proven

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:30.489
once you succeed at killing the Great Carp with Harunaga's poisonous bait

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:36.400
During the pot noble quest line. Once it's fed return here and you'll find its corpse

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:44.020
Proof that somehow a corpse even as large as this one can end up here. Speaking of the depths

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:48.280
I always found this piece of dialogue strange where the old woman asks

00:09:48.280 --> 00:09:55.420
whether you'll be cast out or throw yourself in and as I was scanning through all the dialogue text that was data mined for the

00:09:55.420 --> 00:09:58.539
Game, I actually discovered this cut line from Kuro

00:09:58.540 --> 00:10:04.899
It reads "There exists a great Gorge into which immortals are cast away into the Underworld".

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:12.729
Obviously he's talking about the Ashina Depths and we do find many undying down here, some of them victims of

00:10:13.310 --> 00:10:15.310
experiments with the rejuvenating waters.

00:10:15.950 --> 00:10:18.910
Speaking of cut content down here. Originally

00:10:18.910 --> 00:10:22.389
There was a different item you gave to the red priest of Mibu Village.

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:27.999
Instead of Dragon's Spring Sake it was supposed to be a fresh Innsmouth liver

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:35.229
And this is significant because the town of Innsmouth is the setting for H.P.Lovecraft's "Shadow Over

00:10:35.230 --> 00:10:41.590
Innsmouth" and in this story members of the village are turning into horrific aquatic life forms

00:10:41.930 --> 00:10:46.070
Which not only bears a ton of similarity to events in Mibu

00:10:46.320 --> 00:10:54.200
But this is the story that inspired the Fishing Hamlets in Bloodborne, and there exists even more overlap with Bloodborne's fishing village.

00:10:54.510 --> 00:11:00.649
Slugs for example are a part of the story and environment in Mibu, just as they're a huge part of Bloodborne's

00:11:00.870 --> 00:11:08.270
Fishing Hamlet. The basket-head also mentions a hunter named Inuhiko, an outcast who eats the flesh of beasts and

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:13.339
Who uses fire to ward away other villagers just like the hunters do in Bloodborne.

00:11:13.339 --> 00:11:17.989
I think it's less of an easter egg and more of yet another example of

00:11:18.270 --> 00:11:23.989
From Software having common elements across all their games, not to mention the vermin in Bloodborne.

00:11:24.360 --> 00:11:28.039
Which have their own counterparts in Sekiro's centipedes.

00:11:28.170 --> 00:11:33.500
There's even a hanging man cradling something that looks like a humanity sprite here

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:36.320
Perhaps he was killed for holding on to his humanity

00:11:36.600 --> 00:11:37.560
which is

00:11:37.560 --> 00:11:44.869
Clearly something that the other villagers have abandoned. One thing that we never really got to the bottom of was why Mibu Lake is filled

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:51.770
With the upturned bodies of the villagers. The most logical reason is that they drowned this way due to their undying thirst

00:11:52.470 --> 00:11:56.060
but a more satisfying explanation lies in the

00:11:56.790 --> 00:12:04.250
1976 Japanese film "The Inugamis" which features a murder victim who was found in a lake in this exact same

00:12:04.709 --> 00:12:07.579
upturned pose and if I understand correctly

00:12:07.680 --> 00:12:13.880
this is something that has been referenced in more Japanese media than just Sekiro since then, and

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:19.190
We have "the sarcastic Canadian" on Reddit to thank for catching this one.

00:12:19.890 --> 00:12:25.849
Moving back up to the mountains and valleys of Ashina. We look next to an item within Senpou Temple

00:12:25.850 --> 00:12:30.409
It's a second bell just like the one that takes us to the illusory holes

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:35.209
This one is found in the lower part of Senpou, in the room with the centipede long neck

00:12:35.209 --> 00:12:41.869
and you have to wonder if this was ever meant to serve a purpose, an entry point to a future DLC, pheraphs.

00:12:42.510 --> 00:12:48.379
One of the most interesting items in Sekiro is the contact medicine, a consumable that allows the player to

00:12:48.839 --> 00:12:54.549
Voluntarily inflict a weak poison upon themselves so that they can't be affected by stronger poisons

00:12:54.549 --> 00:13:01.300
But it's most interesting use actually pertains to the mist Raven prosthetic, for once you've taken the poison

00:13:01.640 --> 00:13:09.000
Allows you to dash at any time, since you're always taking damage and if you look carefully at the contact medicine you'll discover

00:13:09.009 --> 00:13:12.980
what's responsible for your affliction. Stemming from the powder crushed into

00:13:13.310 --> 00:13:17.860
tiny little bits, are wings and abdomens of what can only be

00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:20.240
wasps or bees.

00:13:20.240 --> 00:13:22.660
Next is something incredibly cool

00:13:22.850 --> 00:13:28.869
But also incredibly unknown if you use the bestowal ninjutsu on the green lizards

00:13:28.940 --> 00:13:35.230
Then your blade becomes enhanced with poisonous properties and the same goes for blood smoke. You conjure a green

00:13:35.230 --> 00:13:39.879
Mist that will poison anything inside of it. The lizards are so easy to kill that

00:13:39.880 --> 00:13:45.130
No one ever thinks to waste ninjutsu on them, but these effects are incredible and honestly

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:49.869
It's actually a huge shame that these lizards are always placed in out-of-the-way locations

00:13:50.330 --> 00:13:52.989
Imagine if they were placed within boss fights for example

00:13:52.990 --> 00:13:56.770
And you could actually poison bosses by taking out a lizard at a key moment

00:13:56.770 --> 00:14:04.059
I feel like this ninjutsu could actually give you an edge in those fights. The same principle applies to the white lizards.

00:14:04.060 --> 00:14:06.880
Of course though the effect is way harder to figure out

00:14:07.460 --> 00:14:08.980
after a ton of experimenting

00:14:08.980 --> 00:14:13.269
I realized that the Stowell actually imbues your blade with a lifesteal effect

00:14:13.270 --> 00:14:17.650
And that the blood smoke can be used to conjure a health

00:14:18.170 --> 00:14:19.340
regenerating cloud

00:14:19.340 --> 00:14:22.239
but you'll never need to heal if you never take damage and

00:14:22.550 --> 00:14:28.029
There's no way to take no damage more stylish than the Senpou Kick into high monk

00:14:28.070 --> 00:14:29.810
It actually deals really

00:14:29.810 --> 00:14:31.810
fantastic amount of posture damage if

00:14:31.940 --> 00:14:38.320
You use it as an anti sweep attack because it also gets the bonus for jumping onto an enemy as well

00:14:38.330 --> 00:14:45.730
Just don't use it when your enemies are equipped with projectiles as you'll take extra damage and get smacked out of the air

00:14:46.040 --> 00:14:50.349
Of course this principle applies to your enemies as well every time they're in the air

00:14:50.630 --> 00:14:56.980
Make sure you throw a shuriken or you can even throw ceramic shards to knock enemies out of the air

00:14:56.980 --> 00:15:04.169
this might be one of the most underrated items in the whole game. Speaking of anti-air death blows, a

00:15:04.690 --> 00:15:07.320
Surprising amount of enemies are susceptible to them

00:15:07.630 --> 00:15:13.349
There's the Twin Blade enemies, the Okami, but most useful is actually against the Shichimen Warrior.

00:15:13.570 --> 00:15:21.029
You may not have realized that you can use this here though because it only becomes possible to do if you have divined confetti

00:15:21.250 --> 00:15:27.630
Active on your weapon. Confetti is also an item that's generally underrated especially in the late game and New Game+

00:15:27.880 --> 00:15:33.209
Where you can purchase an infinite supply after getting the dragon's tally board from the corrupted monk

00:15:33.610 --> 00:15:38.070
It's the best item to spend your zen on at that point because divine confetti

00:15:38.470 --> 00:15:43.350
Actually increases your weapon damage against all enemies not just apparitions

00:15:43.420 --> 00:15:51.029
this item allows you to connect with apparition type enemies because the paper is created using water from The Fountainhead and

00:15:51.250 --> 00:15:53.880
Its blessed by the gods and this got me thinking

00:15:54.490 --> 00:16:02.339
Well, then how come you can damage the headless underwater without the confetti then. One answer might be that since they're underwater

00:16:02.339 --> 00:16:06.389
In the same divine waters that created the divine confetti

00:16:06.730 --> 00:16:10.769
They might naturally be vulnerable to it as a result

00:16:11.380 --> 00:16:18.089
Moving on down into the valley you encounter this League of snipers who can take you out at an insane distance

00:16:18.220 --> 00:16:23.250
And what I love in this area is just the attention to detail even with the whipping winds

00:16:23.350 --> 00:16:29.640
These snipers are still able to hit you and the reason is these. These I think are called wind socks

00:16:29.680 --> 00:16:35.579
Which allow you to tell which direction wind is blowing and how fast all at a glance.

00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:42.269
This is an invaluable tool for the snipers of the Sunken Valley. And damn, those snipers sound pretty OP, right?

00:16:42.430 --> 00:16:42.970
well

00:16:42.970 --> 00:16:48.930
What if I told you that you could recruit one of them for your own. I found this idea on YouTube and it's pretty genius.

00:16:49.149 --> 00:16:56.219
You just use puppeteer on the snake eyes, right outside the guardian ape fog gate and you can actually bring her in with you as

00:16:56.860 --> 00:17:00.329
Ranged support during this difficult 2v2 fight.

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:07.229
Just make sure you reapply the effect throughout the fight and the fight against the two Apes actually ends up being much more fair

00:17:07.569 --> 00:17:09.569
Something people rarely do is

00:17:09.579 --> 00:17:13.589
Kill the Guardian Ape before you kill the Guardian Ape's low health mate

00:17:13.589 --> 00:17:17.638
If you do this, then you actually don't need to even kill the mate

00:17:17.739 --> 00:17:24.509
She just gets sad and leaves instead. This next theory was put forward by a Japanese blogger

00:17:24.509 --> 00:17:26.939
There's a translated link in the description

00:17:27.059 --> 00:17:31.768
It puts forward that years ago Ashina might have been hit by a meteorite

00:17:32.080 --> 00:17:32.980
made of

00:17:32.980 --> 00:17:36.569
Adamantite, which would explain the precious metal scraps that

00:17:36.669 --> 00:17:43.709
Ashina is known for as well as this deep lake that's right in the middle of the Fountainhead. To add to this

00:17:43.710 --> 00:17:51.419
I would put forward that Lazulite, the rare metal of Fountainhead Palace, also would have come from this meteorite as well,

00:17:51.639 --> 00:17:59.399
because the last line of the lazulite shuriken actually reads "the lazulite blue trail of light it emits in flight, is

00:17:59.619 --> 00:18:03.719
reminiscent the shooting star". This meteor would explain a few things

00:18:04.059 --> 00:18:10.709
It would explain why the metals of the Ashina are so special, so special that they attracted the attention of the gods.

00:18:10.960 --> 00:18:14.489
It would explain the supernatural powers of the divine waters and

00:18:14.950 --> 00:18:22.049
Perhaps most importantly, it would explain why the Mibu breathing technique was required to meet the Divine Dragon.

00:18:22.419 --> 00:18:27.508
The path to the palace is underwater after all, but it can't have always been this way.

00:18:27.519 --> 00:18:32.368
The crater must have filled with water after the arrival of the Divine Dragon.

00:18:33.129 --> 00:18:36.509
Right before meeting the Divine Dragon we find what is

00:18:37.119 --> 00:18:43.858
surely a Miko, a sort of female shaman or shrine maiden. And if my research is correct

00:18:44.289 --> 00:18:48.539
then their role was one of spirit possession and cleansing and

00:18:49.029 --> 00:18:53.219
she may have even served as a means of communication with the divine,

00:18:53.860 --> 00:19:00.720
allowing the dragon to possess and speak through her. You can make a very strong case for both mortal blades

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:03.240
originating from the divine realm.

00:19:03.320 --> 00:19:06.200
The "Open Gate" or "Black Mortal Blade" has a

00:19:06.200 --> 00:19:14.280
description that asks the user to make offerings to the Dragon's blood, and the "Gracious Gift of Tears" or "Red Mortal Blade" was

00:19:14.499 --> 00:19:19.589
surely intended for use on the Divine Dragon, because it gets its tears. Though

00:19:19.590 --> 00:19:22.439
It's impossible to know why it was created.

00:19:22.659 --> 00:19:29.099
If you look at the box  it comes from actually you can even see the same crest commonly found in Fountainhead Palace.

00:19:29.649 --> 00:19:35.699
Furthermore the Red Mortal Blade was taken and hidden by the Senpou High Priest, the man who

00:19:36.100 --> 00:19:38.819
founded Senpou Temple, meaning that the man himself

00:19:39.370 --> 00:19:45.779
surely once traveled to this palace. A fact that makes sense when you look at the similarity in

00:19:46.090 --> 00:19:48.090
architecture between these two places.

00:19:48.730 --> 00:19:52.980
That's what I love about From Software's games. Their world building is just so

00:19:53.559 --> 00:19:58.229
consistent and it's beyond to compare. While exploring the Fountainhead,

00:19:58.389 --> 00:20:04.739
it's easy to become enfeebled, likely leading to a quick death as you can't even resurrect in this state

00:20:05.169 --> 00:20:07.258
However, you can still fight back

00:20:07.779 --> 00:20:12.059
barely, and if you manage to inflict a death blow upon an opponent

00:20:12.059 --> 00:20:18.268
you actually undergo a unique kill animation in your weakened state. While recording this death blow

00:20:18.269 --> 00:20:23.609
I managed to get a closer look at one of the crests on the palace noble scarves.

00:20:23.769 --> 00:20:29.758
It's a picture of the Vermilion Bird, something that's mentioned a couple more times in game.

00:20:30.309 --> 00:20:35.849
Nearby is the Vermillion Bridge where you fight the Corrupted Monk, and it's also emblazoned upon

00:20:36.340 --> 00:20:42.539
Suzaku's Lotus Umbrella, which protects you from flame. But what exactly is the Vermilion Bird?

00:20:42.909 --> 00:20:47.369
Well put simply it's basically the eastern version of the Phoenix

00:20:47.440 --> 00:20:54.299
It's a red pheasant that is perpetually covered in flame, a mythological spirit creature of the Chinese

00:20:54.759 --> 00:21:00.149
Constellations. Another cultural reference nearby is the mask that's worn by the Corrupted Monk

00:21:00.730 --> 00:21:03.029
Specifically this is actually called a Han'nya mask

00:21:03.399 --> 00:21:08.758
Something that's used to represent a jealous female demon in Japanese noir theater

00:21:08.759 --> 00:21:14.639
It has a wonderful design because when you look at it straight on it's meant to look frightening and angry

00:21:14.860 --> 00:21:17.279
But when you look at it from an above angle

00:21:17.279 --> 00:21:21.989
the face is sorrowful and it's a design that's intended to convey the

00:21:22.320 --> 00:21:24.560
complexities of human emotion.

00:21:24.560 --> 00:21:31.320
Another cultural reference is the Great Carp, which could pertain to the Chinese legend of the Dragon's Gate. As the story goes

00:21:31.320 --> 00:21:33.740
Many carp swim upstream in the rivers current

00:21:33.970 --> 00:21:40.959
but very few are brave enough to make that final leap over the waterfall to the Dragon's Gate. If a carp

00:21:41.210 --> 00:21:45.490
successfully makes the jump it can transform into a powerful dragon and

00:21:46.070 --> 00:21:53.919
considering the Divine Dragon is actually called the "Ningyo Dragon" in cut content and the word Ningyo describes a sort of carp

00:21:54.140 --> 00:21:59.949
We can put stock in this legend, as it relates to the Divine Dragon. And speaking of the carp

00:22:00.020 --> 00:22:05.739
did you know that it's possible to make it friendly if you feed him Koremori's truly precious bait

00:22:05.900 --> 00:22:09.789
then he'll no longer attack you in the underwater stealth section.

00:22:10.460 --> 00:22:15.850
Another beast in the Fountainhead Palace is the Sakura bull, roaming at the back of the area.

00:22:16.160 --> 00:22:23.170
Since this isn't actually a boss fight like the other bull fight, you can use the Firecracker from stealth here, which

00:22:23.690 --> 00:22:27.760
scares the bull to death, literally. While all this is going on below

00:22:27.760 --> 00:22:35.260
I also want to point out that the Okami on the rooftops are just chillin and enjoying their sake. Anyway back to the bull.

00:22:35.720 --> 00:22:40.449
Scaring it completely breaks the bulls posture something that can never happen to you

00:22:40.450 --> 00:22:43.000
as long as you deflect the attack.

00:22:43.490 --> 00:22:49.209
Sure, your posture backhand fill even when you deflect perfectly. Some attacks are just too powerful

00:22:49.460 --> 00:22:56.710
But as long as you deflect them nothing will ever actually break your posture meter, a fact that is particularly

00:22:56.990 --> 00:23:02.620
Important in New Game+. And that's something I've never actually mentioned on the channel. New Game+

00:23:02.930 --> 00:23:10.060
Brings with it the option to give back Kuros' charm, an item that he slips on to your person at the start of the game.

00:23:10.160 --> 00:23:10.880
Without it

00:23:10.880 --> 00:23:15.880
You actually take about 30% chip damage whenever you block against attacks

00:23:16.040 --> 00:23:19.150
So playing in this way requires you to deflect

00:23:19.460 --> 00:23:26.439
perfectly if you want to get by. Another item you might have taken for granted is the Hidden Tooth or the Bite Down Drunk

00:23:26.600 --> 00:23:32.770
Both of which grant you death. However, it's not a regular sort of death. Usually when you die

00:23:32.810 --> 00:23:39.130
Your resurrections are afflicted by a black strike through, which prevents you from resurrecting for a time.

00:23:39.530 --> 00:23:40.030
However

00:23:40.030 --> 00:23:42.370
if you commit sudoku with this item

00:23:42.370 --> 00:23:46.399
You actually get no such black strike., meaning that a player who

00:23:46.739 --> 00:23:52.098
accepts their death with a little bit of foresight can actually squeeze out more resurrections

00:23:52.409 --> 00:23:58.669
especially if you have extra resurrections granted by the Sakura Droplet, that drops from Lady Butterfly.

00:23:58.889 --> 00:23:59.789
Speaking of death

00:23:59.789 --> 00:24:05.358
It was originally planned that NPCs with Dragonrot could die. A mechanic that

00:24:05.669 --> 00:24:07.669
thankfully never made it into the game.

00:24:07.830 --> 00:24:13.939
This was discovered again by Lance McDonald, whose video on the topic you can find in the description and

00:24:14.309 --> 00:24:18.439
he talks about how there used to be an item called Dragonrot Pellets,

00:24:18.629 --> 00:24:23.959
which you could create via Emma by trading in some of your resurrective power.

00:24:24.419 --> 00:24:30.949
Giving these pellets to a sick NPC would heal them but just imagine how tedious this would have been

00:24:31.229 --> 00:24:38.598
compared to the cure-all item we have in the Dragon's Blood Droplet. Another great asset to the community is named

00:24:38.820 --> 00:24:44.929
Illusory Wall who always discovers really neat things about these games. Long ago

00:24:44.929 --> 00:24:48.228
he discovered that if you spam buttons while you're grabbed

00:24:48.389 --> 00:24:53.539
you'll take significantly less damage. One more mechanic that did make it into the game

00:24:53.639 --> 00:24:59.539
but that not many know about is a method by which you increase your stealth when you fall from a high place.

00:25:00.239 --> 00:25:06.619
Crouch as soon as you hit the ground and you'll be able to better stealth past enemies like this one, even from above.

00:25:06.869 --> 00:25:09.649
Speaking of above, the award for the highest kill

00:25:09.960 --> 00:25:15.139
Goes to Evil Plan Z on Reddit who says "Fuck this monkey in particular"

00:25:18.020 --> 00:25:21.960
My final fact pertains to the Sekiro design works

00:25:21.960 --> 00:25:27.700
which is this book of gorgeous art that you can pick up pretty easily online from sites like YESASIA

00:25:27.700 --> 00:25:30.979
and Amazon. Links are in the description, go check it out.

00:25:30.979 --> 00:25:37.459
It's an amazing collector's item, but there aren't too many revelations in here compared to previous design works

00:25:38.309 --> 00:25:44.478
Except for one interesting piece of what must be cut content, which depicts what appears to be Emma

00:25:45.119 --> 00:25:52.098
Her eyes are bound and her hair is graying, in the same manner that Owl's, Kuro and the Okami saw.

00:25:52.349 --> 00:25:54.349
Thank you as always for watching.

00:25:54.389 --> 00:25:56.598
Back in March when Sekiro released

00:25:56.599 --> 00:26:02.439
I first promoted Demon VaatiVidya, my first piece of merch and you guys really liked it

00:26:02.590 --> 00:26:05.980
so now as we wind down Sekiro content

00:26:05.990 --> 00:26:11.020
I'm doing a limited edition sunset version where Vaati is equipped with a katana

00:26:11.450 --> 00:26:17.830
You can only purchase this in the next 48 hours. And from then on you'll be the only ones who own it.

00:26:17.830 --> 00:26:20.140
So if you like the content I make and

00:26:20.299 --> 00:26:24.969
more importantly, if you like the design then go and check it out in the description below.

00:26:25.309 --> 00:26:32.949
It's really heartening to have you all still supporting what I do. So, thank you so much, and I'll see you next time.

00:26:41.270 --> 00:26:43.270
 

